 ### `--expand-div`
 If you need `maspsx` to expand `div/divu` and `rem/remu` ops, pass `--expand-div` to `maspsx`. There is already handling for partial div expansion (i.e. where `-0` was passed to `ASPSX.EXE`).
+
+### `--expand-div-zero-only`
+Expand `div`/`rem` (and `divu`/`remu`) with the **divide-by-zero guard only**, omitting the signed-overflow check that `--expand-div` adds. The `div`/`divu` is followed immediately by its `mfhi`/`mflo`, the zero check, and the `break 0x0,0x7` guard:
+
+```
+div	$zero,$v0,$s0
+mfhi	$s1
+bnez	$s0,.L_NOT_DIV_BY_ZERO_<n>
+nop
+break	0x0,0x7
+.L_NOT_DIV_BY_ZERO_<n>:
+```
+
+This matches retail PSY-Q output where the compiler emitted only the zero-division guard (e.g. Digimon Rumble Arena `st05` `func_800D4D54`). If both `--expand-div` and `--expand-div-zero-only` are passed, the narrower `--expand-div-zero-only` wins.
 
 ### `--macro-inc`
 Get `maspsx` to add an `include "macro.inc"` statement to the output.
